        "id": 142165,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-05-27T15:31:40.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Natediggadoggity\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/f04885/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Natediggadoggity:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Does anyone else feel like the Card Version is suddenly more acccessible now they've played the video game for a while?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Having built up my knowledge of the decks one game/expansion at a time, it's been a long, long time since I felt overwhelmed by the sheer amount of knowledge one needs in order to play fluidly w/out having to learn a lot from most of the cards. So, no, the video game didn't make the card game more accessible for me, but I could certainly see how it might for someone newer to the game.</p>",
